SRC/choose -- choose, as built for OS-9/68000=============================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.unix carried it: README, choose.1 andchoose.c.  choose.c here differs from it only inside #ifdef OSK:  - <sys/time.h> and gettimeofday() give way to <time.h> and time(), which    seeds the generator from the clock in whole seconds, as tv_sec did.  - random() and srandom() are rand() and srand(); /dd/LIB/rand.r supplies    them, as the recipe says.  - the temporary file is /dd/tmp/chooseXXXXXX, not /tmp/choose.XXXXXX,    and it is removed again before choose exits.Two runs in the same second pick the same lines, as they did on Unix.